REFERENCE   6  (bases 1 to 1555)
  AUTHORS   Christman,S.A., Kong,B.W., Landry,M.M., Kim,H. and Foster,D.N.
  TITLE     Contributions of differential p53 expression in the spontaneous
            immortalization of a chicken embryo fibroblast cell line
  JOURNAL   BMC Cell Biol 7, 27 (2006)
   PUBMED   16813656
  REMARK    GeneRIF: An initial down-regulation of p53 allowed the SC-2 cells
            to bypass senescence. The inactivation of p53, and consequently
            p21WAF1, likely contributed to the SC-2 cells becoming a fully
            immortal cell line.
REFERENCE   7  (bases 1 to 1555)
  AUTHORS   Takagi,M., Takeda,T., Asada,Y., Sugimoto,C., Onuma,M. and Ohashi,K.
  TITLE     The presence of a short form of p53 in chicken lymphoblastoid cell
            lines during apoptosis
  JOURNAL   J Vet Med Sci 68 (6), 561-566 (2006)
   PUBMED   16820712
  REMARK    GeneRIF: results suggest that the short form of p53 could play a
            role in the initiation of apoptosis induced by the chemotherapeutic
            compound, and that the regulation of its expression may be
            important for the maintenance of transformation status.
REFERENCE   8  (bases 1 to 1555)
  AUTHORS   Trtkova,K. and Plachy,J.
  TITLE     Deletions in the DNA-binding domain of the TP53 gene in
            v-src-transformed chicken cells
  JOURNAL   In Vitro Cell Dev Biol Anim 40 (8-9), 285-292 (2004)
   PUBMED   15723564
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Results suggest that extensive deletions are efficient
            mechanisms of TP53 inactivation, occurring as early events during
            the immortalization of v-src-transformed chicken cells.
